       title="AZD" id="Azd">

    <link-summary>Documentation for AZD, the Azure DevOps plugin for JetBrains IDEs.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Azure DevOps pull requests, pipelines, boards and AI review in your JetBrains IDE.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>AZD brings Azure DevOps to JetBrains IDEs: clone repositories, review and merge pull requests, run
        and approve pipelines, manage work items and use AI review.</web-summary>

    <section-starting-page>
        <title>AZD</title>
        <description>
            Work with Azure DevOps Services and Azure DevOps Server without leaving your JetBrains IDE.
            Clone repositories, review and merge pull requests, run and approve pipelines, track work items, and use AI to
            write and review changes.
            AZD is a paid plugin with a 10-day free trial.
        </description>

        <spotlight>
            <a href="Azd-Installation.topic" type="start"
               summary="Install AZD and sign in with Microsoft, the Azure CLI or a personal access token">Install and connect</a>
            <a href="Work-with-Azure-DevOps-pull-requests.topic" type="tools"
               summary="Find, filter and open pull requests in the AZD Pull Requests tool window">Work with pull requests</a>
        </spotlight>

        <primary>
            <title>Features</title>
            <a href="Pull-Request-Details.topic" type="integration"
               summary="Read the timeline, check policies and review changed files">Review a pull request</a>
            <a href="Azd-AI.topic" type="development"
               summary="Generate titles, descriptions and commit messages, and review changes with AI">AI assistant</a>
            <a href="Azure-DevOps-Pipelines.topic" type="cloud"
               summary="Run pipelines, inspect runs, read logs and view the stage diagram">Work with pipelines</a>
            <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Yaml.topic" type="development"
               summary="Completion and validation for Azure Pipelines YAML files">Edit Azure Pipelines YAML</a>
            <a href="Azd-Boards.topic" type="tools"
               summary="Find, edit and create work items, and use the Kanban board">Boards and work items</a>
            <a href="Azd-Manage-projects-hosted-on-Azure-DevOps.topic" type="learn"
               summary="Clone repositories and open files on Azure DevOps">Clone and manage projects</a>
        </primary>

        <secondary>
